{"availability":"available","full":"ityonemo/clr","name":"clr","description":"Checker for Lifetimes and other Refinement types","category":"Other","language":"Zig","stars":278,"forks":2,"created":"2025-02-02T21:30:22Z","updated":"2026-07-31T13:36:03Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":null,"color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T16:20:46.576Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T16:20:46.576Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T16:20:46.576Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T16:20:46.576Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T16:20:46.576Z","stars":278,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This project creates a Zig transpiler for the Zig compiler, which transforms AIR (Abstract Intermediate Representation) into Zig source code that performs static analysis at compile time. The generated analyzer catches memory safety issues like use-before-assignment, use-after-free, stack pointer escapes, as well as Zig-specific UB such as non-nullness assertions, tagged union violations, or fieldParentPtr misuse.","The goal is to bring Rust-level memory safety guarantees to Zig through static analysis of AIR, without changing the language itself.","CLR depends on a forked version of the Zig compiler (included as a submodule in zig/) that adds support for routing AIR to external plugins. When invoked with -ofmt=air -fair-out=, the compiler loads the specified shared library and passes generated AIR to it for processing."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ityonemo/clr/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"eb594c34c071c107e2684c35d9d336a5ce8520745a73eb20eff70aa69f9abff6","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T16:20:46.576Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T16:20:46.576Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This project creates a Zig transpiler for the Zig compiler, which transforms AIR (Abstract Intermediate Representation) into Zig source code that performs static analy